# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A required input no one can give is refused where the chain starts, before
# anything runs. r reads zz; the unit does not declare it. withzz has zz 30
# and may call r. The definition f only hands the name on: the zz of the
# method that made f is not f's to give, and r has no source of its own. The
# root that calls f has no zz: that call is refused.
fn: r () int
    return: zz + 1
end: r

fn: withzz () int
    int: zz 30
    return: r()
end: withzz

fn: mk (int: k) fn: () int
    int: zz 50
    fn: f () int
        return: k + r()
    return: f

@: u0 mk(5)
int: b withzz()
int: a u0()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
